WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.510
- I don't know if you've ever noticed this

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.700
but it seems like sometimes in life,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.200
the more you want something,

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.680
the harder it is to get.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.130
This seems to be the case
with starting a business

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.850
or writing a book or any
of these big life plans

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:15.270
we always dream about.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.740
Seems like the more we fantasize

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.950
about these types of things,

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.750
the more we procrastinate
doing anything about them.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.860
But there's a very
specific reason for this

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.830
and it is brilliantly explained

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.430
in probably one of the
best books I have ever read

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:31.060
in my life called, "The War
of Art" by Steven Pressfield.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.200
So in this book, Steven
Pressfield explains that

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.850
there is a psychological
force that is working

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.290
against you every single day of your life

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:42.510
and is intimately involved in
every decision that you make

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:43.980
whether you're aware of it or not.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.890
And the sole purpose of
this force is to keep you

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:50.170
from reaching your potential,
it's called resistance.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:52.330
Now whether we've called
it resistance or not,

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.560
we've all definitely felt
it usually in the form of

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.220
it's sort of internal
tension that you feel

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.850
whenever you think about
doing something constructive

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:03.530
whether it's picking up a
paintbrush to start painting

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:06.450
or opening the Word doc
to start writing the essay

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.130
you've been procrastinating forever,

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:11.310
resistance will be there
to rear its ugly head

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:13.710
because resistance prevents progression.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.500
If there were no such thing as resistance,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.597
we would all be living
according to our highest ideals.

00:01:18.597 --> 00:01:21.430
If we knew it was our
mission to write a book,

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:22.760
we would just start writing.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.890
If we knew that it was
in our best interest

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:28.420
to do cardio, sail faster on
ice when you played hockey,

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.360
we would just do cardio,
whenever we thought of it,

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.030
we would just do cardio, there
would be nothing stopping us.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.230
But unfortunately, every
single time we think

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.200
about doing something constructive,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.280
resistance starts to inject
itself into our being

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.160
without us even realizing it.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.870
It's an automatic process and
it happens every single time.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.250
So for example, pretend you're
wasting time playing X-Box

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.770
or something and you've been
playing for a couple of hours

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:54.940
and the thought dawns
on you to go to the gym

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:58.520
because it's Monday and
Monday's international Chest Day

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.570
or religious holiday and
you really should hit chest,

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:02.880
it's the right thing to do.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.410
But since it's the right thing to do

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:07.430
and it is integral for your
growth as a human being,

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:09.410
at least in that area of life,

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.310
you will encounter resistance.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:15.240
First, it usually takes the
form of physical discomfort.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.750
When you think about going to the gym

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.090
while you're wasting time on X-Box,

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.920
the thought of going to the gym becomes

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.090
very physically uncomfortable.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.820
You start to tense up,
you start to win set

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.450
the thought of doing
something more uncomfortable

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:30.040
than the thing you're currently doing,

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.170
which is interesting
because once you're actually

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.150
at the gym, it's not that bad.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.890
In fact, it's pretty fun and
you feel really fulfilled

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.030
and you feel like you're
accomplishing something

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.260
but in that moment,
when you're wasting time

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.300
going to the gym seems like a monster.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.133
It seems like something you
definitely don't want to do,

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:48.030
that is resistance.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:49.220
And since human beings like

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.280
to stay intellectually consistent,

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.480
resistance will start
to creep into your mind

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.660
in the form of rationalization.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:58.450
You need any sort of good
reason not to encounter

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:01.100
this physical pain of going to the gym.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.750
Maybe you think about the fact that

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.440
since it's Monday and
International Chest Day,

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.340
everybody is going to be
doing chest on Monday.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:10.090
So there's gonna be a huge
lineup for the bench press.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:12.010
Besides, you went to the gym last week

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.290
and it takes a lot longer than one week

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.830
for you to lose all your gains

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.790
and for your muscles to deteriorate

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:20.170
so it's probably not a big deal
if you just skip this week.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.990
You've been pretty good
up until this point

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.550
and you kind of deserve a break.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.010
Maybe you're familiar with this
type of pattern of thinking

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.650
and it's actually really
common and it's resistance

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.370
but here's something I find
a little bit more disturbing.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.120
It seems like the more
important something is

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.340
for your growth as a human being,

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:39.210
the more powerful resistance
will be stopping you

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.043
from doing it.

00:03:40.043 --> 00:03:42.920
A great example of this
is me and this channel.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.030
When I first started
off making these videos,

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:45.960
it was just a hobby.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.030
But as you guys started
watching more and more

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.860
and I've started to develop an audience,

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:52.680
it is now become my
most viable career path.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.140
Sponsors are reaching
out, things are happening,

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.430
the audience is growing and it's great

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:00.900
but because of that fact,
resistance is stronger than ever.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.410
And for me, resistance takes
the form of perfectionism.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.370
Whenever I sit down to write a video,

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:09.300
I always feel like I have
to outdo the last one.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.070
It has to be the perfect video
with the perfect be roll.

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:14.310
And it really becomes
a barrier to uploading

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.870
as frequently as I would like.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:18.230
And as I've started to
reread "The War Art"

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.630
by Steven Pressfield, I start to realize

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:23.040
that this type of thinking
is just resistance.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.000
Resistance never goes away.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.740
You always hear about famous
singers and performers

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.400
and comedians who still get really nervous

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.070
before they go on stage.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.800
They encounter resistance even
though they've been doing it

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.070
for decades even.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:37.510
So what's their response.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.640
So they just not go on stage.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.540
Of course not, their careers will be over

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.717
but what the most
successful people do instead

00:04:43.717 --> 00:04:47.020
is they get really good at
automatically breaking past

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.150
this resistance as it presents itself.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:51.070
And the better you get at doing this,

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:53.780
the more efficient you'll
be at doing the right thing

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.380
instead of the comfortable thing.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.670
Because when you just sit down to write

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.170
or when you just put on the running shoes

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:02.000
or when you just hit record,

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.200
something magical happens,
words start to flow,

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.010
endorphins start to run,

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:10.450
inspiration starts to
magically descend upon you

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.460
and all the pieces sort of fall together.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.511
The proper response to resistance

00:05:14.511 --> 00:05:17.340
is to just start the thing anyways.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:20.480
Once you start realizing that
whatever rationalizations

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.760
you have for not doing the
thing you know you have to do

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.180
is just resistance.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:26.750
You can gain the mental clarity

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:28.570
to just do the thing anyways.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:31.170
And as you become more
familiar with resistance

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:32.930
and seeing it for what it is,

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.810
you can really start to
use resistance as a guide.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.050
Since resistance is most powerful,

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:39.890
the more important something is,

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:43.840
it's a great compass leading
you to where you need to go.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.260
And as you win these
battles with resistance,

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.310
day by day, month by
month and year by year,

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:51.500
the life you live will become bigger

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.160
than the unlived life within you.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.640
And you'll eventually start
living the kind of life

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.203
you actually want to be living.

